18592680



AMENDMENTS TO THE CLAIMS


This listing of claims will replace all prior versions, and listings, of claims in the application.





1. (Currently Amended) An apparatus for artificial intelligence-supported diagnostic assessment, wherein the apparatus comprises:
at least a processor, wherein the processor is configured to:
receive a plurality of multi-channel sensor readings of physiological data;
generate training data correlating each of the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings with a plurality of diagnostic labels;
train a neural network using the plurality of diagnostic labels;
update the training data as a function of new training examples;
retrain the neural network as a function of the updated training data, wherein the retraining occurs when a preconfigured threshold of new training examples is exceeded;
receive a time series input describing user physiological data from at least a sensor;
input the time series input into the trained neural network;
generate diagnostic data as a function of the time series input and the trained neural network, wherein the diagnostic data includes a classification under a plurality of groups, wherein the groups are comprised of:
normal LV function;
LVSD only;
LVDD only; and 
both LVSD and LVDD;
determine prognostic data as a function of the diagnostic data; and
output the prognostic data. 



2. (Original) The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the time series input is comprised of electrocardiogram (ECG) data.



3. (Currently Amended) The apparatus of claim 2, wherein the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings further comprises a plurality of ECG readings, and the plurality of training data further comprises [[a]] the plurality of ECG readings, and generating the plurality of training data further comprises:
receiving echocardiogram data correlated to each ECG reading of the plurality of ECG readings; and 
generating the plurality of diagnostic labels using the echocardiogram data. 



4. (Original) The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the neural network is a multi-output convolutional neural network. 



5. (Currently Amended) The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the neural network is trained using general-use lead data, wherein the general-use lead data refers to the lead data used for a diagnostic tool.



6. (Currently Amended) The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the neural network is trained using reduced general-use lead data, wherein the reduced general-use lead data refers to a reduction in the leads used in acquiring the lead data. 



7. (Currently Amended) The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the neural network is trained [[using]] as a function of lead data gathered from 12-lead ECGs performed within 14 days of transthoracic echocardiography, wherein the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings of physiological data are comprised of the 12-lead ECG data and the lead echocardiography data correlated to each 12-lead ECG datum. 



8. (Original)The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the diagnostic data includes an assessment of LVDD. 



9. (Canceled)



10. (Currently Amended) The apparatus of claim 1, further comprising a display device, wherein the output of prognostic data is displayed at a display device to diagnose a patient. 



11. (Currently Amended) A method for training an artificial intelligence-supported diagnostic assessment tool, wherein the method comprises:
receiving a plurality of multi-channel sensor readings of physiological data;
generating training data correlating each of the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings with a plurality of diagnostic labels;

training a neural network using the plurality of diagnostic labels;
updating the training data as a function of new training examples;
retraining the neural network as a function of the updated training data, wherein the retraining occurs when a preconfigured threshold of new training examples is exceeded;
receiving a time series input describing user physiological data from at least a sensor; 
inputting the time series input into the trained neural network;
generating diagnostic data as a function of the time series input and the trained neural network, wherein the diagnostic data includes a classification under a plurality of groups, wherein the groups are comprised of:
normal LV function;
LVSD only;
LVDD only; and 
both LVSD and LVDD;
determining prognostic data as a function of the diagnostic data; and
outputting the prognostic data. 



12. (Original) The method of claim 11, wherein the time series input is comprised of electrocardiogram (ECG) data.



13. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 12, wherein the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings further comprises a plurality of ECG readings, and the plurality of training data further comprises [[a]] the plurality of ECG readings, and generating the plurality of training data further comprises:
receiving echocardiogram data correlated to each ECG reading of the plurality of ECG readings; and 
generating the plurality of diagnostic labels using the echocardiogram data. 



14. (Original) The method of claim 11, wherein the neural network is a multi-output convolutional neural network. 



15. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 11, wherein the neural network is trained using general-use lead data, wherein the general-use lead data refers to the lead data used for a diagnostic tool.



16. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 11, wherein the neural network is trained using reduced general-use lead data, wherein the reduced general-use lead data refers to a reduction in the leads used in acquiring the lead data. 



17. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 11, wherein the neural network is trained using lead data gathered from 12-lead ECGs performed within 14 days of transthoracic echocardiography, wherein the plurality of multi-channel sensor readings of physiological data are comprised of the 12-lead ECG data and echocardiographythe lead data correlated to each 12-lead ECG datum. 



18. (Original) The method of claim 11, wherein the diagnostic data includes an assessment of both LVSD and LVDD. 



19. (Canceled)



20. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 11, wherein the output of prognostic data ismethod further comprises displaying the output of prognostic datadisplayed at a display device to diagnose a patient. 



21. (New) The apparatus of claim 1, further comprising a sensor for receiving the time series input.



22. (New) The method of claim 11, wherein the method further comprises measuring the time series input via a sensor.
